    "result_text": "The implementation is complete and the full test suite is green (BUILD SUCCESS, 1 test, 0 failures \u2014 `AcceptanceTest` is the only test class; `AcceptanceBase`/`AuditLogCapture` are support classes).\n\n## What I changed\n\nThe spec: *when more than 80 owners have already been created today, include `bulkSignupWarning: true` in the response; otherwise `false`.* I followed the existing per-owner derived-field pattern (like `namesakeCount`), computing the flag at creation and persisting it so it reads back on `GET /api/owners/{id}`:\n\n1. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added `bulkSignupWarning` (readOnly boolean) to the `Owner` response schema, so the generated `OwnerDto` gets the getter/setter and MapStruct maps it automatically.\n\n2. **`Owner.java`** \u2014 added the `bulkSignupWarning` field (`@Column(name = \"bulk_signup_warning\")`) with getter/setter.\n\n3. **`OwnerRestControllerV1.java`** \u2014 added a `BULK_SIGNUP_WARNING_THRESHOLD = 80` constant and set the flag in `addOwner`:\n   ```java\n   owner.setBulkSignupWarning(\n       countOwnersRegisteredOn(effectiveRegistrationDate) > BULK_SIGNUP_WARNING_THRESHOLD);\n   ```\n   This reuses the same `countOwnersRegisteredOn(...)` accumulation path the daily-limit rule uses, evaluated against the business-day-adjusted registration date. The value is always set (never null), so a fresh create returns `false`.\n\n4. **`db/{hsqldb,h2,mysql,postgres}/schema.sql`** \u2014 added the `bulk_signup_warning BOOLEAN` column (tests run on hsqldb; the others are updated for consistency).",
